[b]QLC+ Swiss Knife v1.5.0 — the Doctor now fixes, and a Rig Reducer[/b]

A new release of Swiss Knife, the free companion toolkit for QLC+ 5 workspaces (not affiliated with the QLC+ project).

[list]
[*][b]Workspace Doctor tab[/b] — check your show and fix what you tick into a new file: broken references, scenes that don't set every channel (LTP bleed), strobe/auto programs left on, a scene shared by a button and a chaser, widgets outside their page… and a [b]PANIC RESET that can't reset[/b]: a plain scene at 0 can't darken a look that is still running (dimmer/RGB are HTP), so the fix turns it into a script that stops everything first. A fix report is saved next to the new file.
[*][b]Rig Reducer[/b] — turn a big show into one for a smaller rig: untick the fixtures you won't have; their values, groups, 3D positions, the functions left empty and their buttons/faders are cleaned up; re-patch names and addresses; preview, then save.
[/list]

Your original show file is never changed — every result is a new _v<N+1>.qxw.

Download: [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/releases/tag/v1.5.0]GitHub release v1.5.0[/url] · [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/wiki]Wiki[/url]
